From 79f07332e9c12d6c1803ecd219a4ac3fd8629e33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:25:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] [css] Use document referrer policy for fetching from
 inline CSS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When parsing an inline stylesheet, `CSSStyleSheet::InlineParserContext`
previously constructed the `CSSParserContext` with
`network::mojom::ReferrerPolicy::kDefault`, causing subresource fetches
(such as fonts, images, or SVG resource references) initiated from
`<style>` elements to ignore the owner document's referrer policy.

Instead, snapshot `owner_node_document.GetReferrerPolicy()` when
creating the inline `CSSParserContext` so that inline stylesheets use
the owner document's referrer policy active at parse time. Also guard
`ExecutionContext::GetReferrerPolicy()` when `policy_container_` is
null (e.g. after `TakePolicyContainer()` on a cloned document).

Original patch by estark@chromium.org.

TAG=agy
CONV=0f543df6-f84d-421a-bec5-5db380444d4d

